review_comments:
This might do the job, nonetheless there are a few things worth pointing out:
- calling `getQualifiedTableName` comes at a cost; looking up the db and schema descriptors might end up doing so from storage, even if it's unlikely;
- if `ResolveTableIndex` was able to find the index of a table, then it seems to me that it should have been able to  resolve that table in the first place. The reason I suspect this is because in CRDB, indexes are always defined within a table descriptor and can't exist independently. Looking at the signature of `ResolveTableIndex`, I further suspect that it already returns that qualified table name as its second argument.
